<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm8a-hainan-2026-11-20 ascent</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-18: NET moved from 2026-11-20T11:00:00Z to 2026-11-20T11:59:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 3:59 a.m. PST). LL2 id a2975167-7c6f-4403-99e1-b40df17c8140, status Go (was TBC), window 11:51-12:17Z, last_updated 2026-11-18T08:29:42Z. NOTAM RPHI B5829/26 re-checked: same South China Sea polygon, still daily 1100-1400Z on 20-23 Nov, which covers 11:51-12:17Z. Azimuth stays 142.99 deg (mean bearing to the B5829/26 and B5830/26 centroids). HYDROPAC 3352/26 was not the azimuth used on the previous file (its areas bear 140.17/140.30/140.30 deg) and no newer hazard notice replacing those polygons was found. utc shifted by +3540 s; ECEF geometry unchanged. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 8A Y13 (SatNet LEO Group TBD?, Hainan Commercial LC-1) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
NO public LM-8A time/altitude/velocity table found. Loft: SURROGATE — the same LM-3B typical GTO event table already used for lm8a-wenchang,
  CALT &#x27;LM-3A Series Launch Vehicles User&#x27;s Manual&#x27; Issue 2011, Tables 3-5/3-6 (event time s, flight altitude km, ground range km), liftoff altitude 1.8 km removed.
  Cut at Stage-3 first shutdown T+615.7 s, 202.5 km, 2466.2 km. This is a family stand-in, not an LM-8A profile and not the assumed 700 km insertion.
Source: http://www.georing.biz/usefull/LM-3A%20Series%20Launch%20Vehicles%20User&#x27;s%20Manual%20Issue%202011.pdf
Ground range IS published, so no Rel.Vel split is needed; velocities are d/dt of the interpolated alt/range (rel_vel = |v| ground-relative).
One horizontal assumption: LM-3B&#x27;s published ground range is laid along this mission&#x27;s constant-azimuth rhumb (LM-3B itself doglegs). Spherical rhumb, R=6371.0088 km.
Az 142.99 deg = mean of great-circle bearings from the pad to the area centroids of NOTAM RPHI B5829/26 (142.920 deg, centroid 12.7558N 116.1662E, 944 km)
  and B5830/26 (143.061 deg, centroid 8.1762N 119.4216E, 1565 km). Mean 142.990 deg. Notices: daily 1100-1400Z, 20-23 Nov 2026.
  Sources: https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-RPHI-B5829%2F26 and https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-RPHI-B5830%2F26
HYDROPAC 3352/26 (and NAVAREA XI 26-0515, same polygons; debris 20 Nov 1000-1600Z, South China Sea + Sulu Sea) bears 140.17/140.30/140.30 deg to areas A/B/C.
  That corridor is about 2.7 deg east of the NOTAM line and is NOT the azimuth used here. Text: https://www.sealagom.com/coastal/21/message/55606/3352-26-south-china-sea/
PRE-FLIGHT. LL2 id a2975167-7c6f-4403-99e1-b40df17c8140, status TBC, NET 2026-11-20T11:00:00Z (Fri 20 Nov 3:00 a.m. PST), window 11:00-14:00Z.
  Mission text: a batch of 9 LEO communications satellites for China SatNet. Flight number Y13 from The Space Road (16 Nov Beijing time, moved to pad 1).
Pad (LL2 Commercial LC-1): 19.597275N 110.930753E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=142.99 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-20T11:59:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description><Placemark><name>Pad (lm8a-hainan-2026-11-20)</name><Point><coordinates>110.9307530,19.5972750,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ascent polyline</name><LineString><altitudeMode>absolute</altitudeMode><tessellate>0</tessellate><coordinates>110.9307530,19.5972750,0 110.9462673,19.5778854,2048 110.9617854,19.5584885,4096 110.9772959,19.5390989,6144 110.9928103,19.5197021,8192 111.0083171,19.5003125,10240 111.0238278,19.4809156,12288 111.0393309,19.4615260,14336 111.0548378,19.4421292,16384 111.0703372,19.4227395,18432 111.0858405,19.4033427,20480 111.1013362,19.3839531,22528 111.1168357,19.3645563,24575 111.1323277,19.3451666,26623 111.1478236,19.3257698,28671 111.1633119,19.3063802,30719 111.1788041,19.2869834,32767 111.1942888,19.2675937,34815 111.2097716,19.2482041,36863 111.2252583,19.2288073,38911 111.2407374,19.2094176,40959 111.2562205,19.1900208,43007 111.2716960,19.1706312,45055 111.2871754,19.1512344,47103 111.3026473,19.1318447,49151 111.3181231,19.1124479,51199 111.3596311,19.0604119,54868 111.4247655,18.9787240,59743 111.4898680,18.8970362,64618 111.5553791,18.8147954,69500 111.6342222,18.7157646,73949 111.7150471,18.6141845,78225 111.7958237,18.5126043,82500 111.8765523,18.4110242,86775 111.9572333,18.3094440,91051 112.0378670,18.2078639,95326 112.1184537,18.1062837,99601 112.1989937,18.0047036,103877 112.2794874,17.9031234,108152 112.3599292,17.8015504,112428 112.4403309,17.6999703,116703 112.5206872,17.5983901,120978 112.6009982,17.4968100,125254 112.6812645,17.3952298,129529 112.7924626,17.2544108,132259 112.9048674,17.1119544,134924 113.0171862,16.9694980,137590 113.1294198,16.8270417,140255 113.2415690,16.6845853,142921 113.3536290,16.5421361,145586 113.4656120,16.3996797,148252 113.5775130,16.2572233,150917 113.6893329,16.1147669,153583 113.8010726,15.9723105,156248 113.9127271,15.8298613,158913 11